(3637, 'Vendeur Gros', 'https://marocemploi.net/offre/vendeur-gros/', 'Maroc Emploi', '2024-12-12', NULL, NULL, NULL, '@ EMID', NULL, 'Nous recrutons un Vendeur Gros pour rejoindre notre équipe dynamique. En tant que vendeur en gros, vous serez responsable de la gestion des ventes, de la négociation avec les clients professionnels, ainsi que de l’atteinte des objectifs commerciaux. Missions principales : Assurer la vente de produits en gros auprès de clients professionnels (commerçants, entreprises, etc.). Conseiller et fidéliser les clients en leur proposant des solutions adaptées à leurs besoins. Négocier les prix et conditions de vente avec les clients. Suivre les commandes, préparer les devis et gérer les livraisons. Analyser le marché et identifier de nouvelles opportunités de vente. Participer à la gestion des stocks et à la présentation des produits en magasin. Assurer un excellent service client et un suivi après-vente. Profil recherché : Expérience significative (minimum 2 années) dans la vente en gros , secteur agroalimentaire. Bonne maîtrise des techniques de vente et de négociation. Excellentes compétences en communication et relationnel client. Sens de l’organisation, rigueur et autonomie. Capacité à travailler sous pression et à atteindre des objectifs commerciaux. Une connaissance des produits [secteur spécifique : alimentaire, équipement, etc.] est un plus.', NULL, 'Casablanca, Casablanca, 20000', 'Agro-alimentaire', NULL, 'CDI', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(3638, 'Offre de Stage : Assistante ADV – Département Logistique', 'https://marocemploi.net/offre/offre-de-stage-assistante-adv-departement-logistique/', 'Maroc Emploi', '2024-12-12', NULL, NULL, NULL, '@ société de distribution', NULL, 'Nous recherchons une stagiaire pour intégrer le département Logistique en tant qu’Assistante ADV, pour une durée allant de 3 à 6 mois. Le transport est assuré La présentation d’une convention de stage est obligatoire. Missions principales : Gestion des commandes clients gros Suivi de la documentation Classement et archivage Profil recherché : Niveau d’études : M1 ou M2. Bonne maîtrise des outils bureautiques (Excel, Word, etc.). Capacité à travailler en équipe Si cette opportunité vous intéresse, merci de nous envoyer votre CV en pièce jointe.', NULL, 'Casablanca, BOUSKOURA , 20000', 'Commerces / distribution', NULL, 'Stage', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(3639, 'Responsable Qualité Produit / QHSE Site H/F (Industrie : Matériel de Ligne) – Casablanca (Ain Sebaa)', 'https://marocemploi.net/offre/responsable-assurance-qualite-qhse-site-h-f-industrie-materiel-de-ligne-casablanca-ain-sebaa/', 'Maroc Emploi', '2024-12-12', '2025-01-11', NULL, NULL, '@ Amzil', NULL, 'Entreprise leader du marché, nous recherchons un(e) Responsable Qualité Produit / QHSE Site pour notre activité Matériel de Ligne. Mission : Vous aurez pour mission de déployer, maintenir, surveiller et améliorer la politique QHSE du site, tout en garantissant l’efficacité du processus de contrôle qualité dès la réception matière première jusqu’à la livraison du produit fini, y compris le traitement des non-conformités. Principales Responsabilités : Accompagner les pilotes de processus, et réaliser des revues périodiques process ; Réaliser les audits internes et veiller à l’application des standards QHSE ; Maintenir les certifications, agréments ou homologations (produits) ; Assurer une veille normative, piloter les réceptions clients, ainsi que le traitement de leurs réclamations Piloter les projets QHSE de son site, et être partie prenante dans les projets de développement produit. Profil recherché : De formation Ingénieur en génie industriel, génie électrique, ou en génie des procédés, vous justifiez d’une expérience de 5 ans minimum dans un poste similaire. Compétences requises : Maitrise des normes (Iso9001, 45001, 14001, 50001) Maitrise statistique des procédés MSP, cartes de contrôle, démarche six sigma Maitrise des MRPs et outils de la qualité Maitrise de l’anglais obligatoire : lu, écrit, parlé Rigueur et organisation Leadership et capacité d’adaptation.', NULL, 'Casablanca, Casablanca, 20000', 'Industrie', NULL, 'CDI', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(3640, 'TECHNICIEN Spécialisé dans la fabrication des gaine en tole galvanisé', 'https://marocemploi.net/offre/technicien-specialise-dans-la-fabrication-des-gaine-en-tole-galvanise/', 'Maroc Emploi', '2024-12-11', NULL, NULL, NULL, '@ ELESI', NULL, 'Entreprise a Agadir cherche une technicien spécialisé dans la fabrication des conduits rectangulaires agrafes avec des machine. Avoir une expérience dans le domaine min 4 ans.', NULL, 'Rabat, Rabat, 10160', 'Industrie', NULL, 'CDD', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'bac +2', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(3641, 'QHSE Engineer', 'https://marocemploi.net/offre/qhse-engineer/', 'Maroc Emploi', '2024-12-11', '2025-01-02', NULL, NULL, '@ MOROCCO PRECISION MOULDING', NULL, 'Job advert: QHSE Engineer About the Role We are seeking a Quality, Health & Safety and Environmental (QHSE) Engineer to join our organisation permanently at our Morocco site (MPM- Fibrax Morocco). Reporting to the site Compliance Manager, the QHSE Engineer will be responsible for the proper application of quality, health, safety and environmental (QHSE) standards within the organisation. This role involves providing support to customers and ensuring the claim analysis and corrective actions implementation follow up within the due dates and achieve quality targets of the Fibrax group of companies. Key responsibilities include: Management of customers claims including Fulfilment of customer portals and manage meetings with customers. Manage the Company’s Non-conformance Reporting System and ensure that root causes are identified, and robust corrective actions implemented to prevent recurrence Ensure that all nonconforming products is properly dispositioned & root cause analysis is performed in line with company procedures (8D,5Whys, Ishikawa…). Management of suppliers claims and PPAP documentation Follow up quality action plans and ensure they are carried out as required. Assistance with both internal and external audits of the compliance management systems. Provision of guidance to relevant departments in the development of process and other improvement programmes. Collaborate with cross-functional teams from different departments to meet quality objectives. Identification of trainings needed for employees regarding customer special characteristics as well as HSE and legal characteristics. Other relevant tasks are requested from time to time. About the Person The successful candidate will be in a quality role and will have established problem solving and communication skills, including managing conflict and facilitating discussions to achieve a constructive outcome. Persistence, organisation, an eye for detail, and the ability to process and prioritise complex information are also key skills. An engineering degree is required. Knowledge/Experience: At least 2 years of experience in a similar role within a manufacturing environment, with a strong focus on process improvement and product quality. Preferably from the automotive industry. Comprehensive understanding of quality management systems and standards such as ISO9001, IATF 16949, and ISO14001. A background in engineering, science, or a related technical field is preferred. Familiarity with Six Sigma, LEAN manufacturing principles, and quality improvement methodologies is beneficial. Solid experience using quality tools such as FMEA, Control Plans, SPC and MSA to drive process optimization and product quality. Strong problem-solving skills with the ability to conduct investigations, identify root causes, and implement corrective actions to prevent recurrence. Excellent communication skills with the ability to work cross-functionally and with customers to resolve quality issues. Attention to detail, critical thinking, and the ability to manage multiple tasks in a fastpaced environment. Strong verbal and written communication skills in English (additional languages are a plus). Proficient in Microsoft Office applications (Excel, Word, PowerPoint) and quality software/tools. About Fibrax Group Fibrax Limited was established in London in 1902 as a manufacturer of bicycle clutch and brake linings. The company enjoyed steady growth and was bought by the current owners, the O’Brien family, in 1975 with a vision to expand and move into new industrial markets. As the cycling division extended its product range, new opportunities simultaneously arose in the automotive and industrial sectors, which resulted in the company investing in new manufacturing headquarters in Wrexham, North Wales. By 1985, Fibrax was operating as a highly successful rubber and plastics injection moulding company supplying quality components worldwide. With the rise of global demand, our facility in Wrexham underwent several extensions to accommodate new equipment. In 2004, we acquired a new, state-of-the-art manufacturing facility in Poland and have since forged production partnerships in Morocco and Turkey. In 2018, we acquired a new manufacturing facility in Berrechid-Morocco. Looking ahead, to enhance operational efficiency and better serve our expanding customer base, we are excited to announce that the facility in Morocco will be transferred to a newly built facility being developed in Kenitra Atlantic Freezone. As a family-owned business, we know our people are critical to the success of our continued growth. We therefore support our employees by providing regular training and opportunities for development. By combining their knowledge and understanding with our latest equipment and machinery, we are able to consistently produce high performance components. As such, Fibrax operates as a highly responsive, full service global manufacturer of polymeric mouldings and assemblies. About the Benefits In addition to a competitive salary depends on experience, you will have access to the following benefits: CIMR. Flexible working hours with flexi time options. Bonuses depend on site evolution. Private medical insurance. Salary development based on performance. If you’re seeking a challenging and rewarding career as part of an extraordinary business with ambitious plans, then what are you waiting for? Apply now. Closing date is 02/01/2025- may close before if high volume applications are received.', NULL, 'Berrechid, Berrechid, 20150', 'Automobile', NULL, 'CDI', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Voir Job Description', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
